# Practice Section Content

Timed retrieval drills organised by grammatical structure. The practice surface is the production-skill engine of the app: Skill Acquisition Theory (DeKeyser) procedural-fluency training, pushing learners from explicit knowledge to procedural skill to automatisation.

Every route under `/practice` needs a session: `route.tsx` `beforeLoad` redirects a logged-out visitor to `/`. The anonymous drill is `/try` (`src/routes/try.tsx`), which reuses `<Drill>`.

## Route Structure

```
/practice                                        Landing: four group links
/practice/review                                 Drills due for review, by category
/practice/cases                                  Case-system index (4 phases)
/practice/cases/{nominative,accusative,genitive}/{article,noun,adjective,phrase}
/practice/cases/review/{articles,nouns,adjectives,phrases}
/practice/pronouns                               Pronoun index (flat list)
/practice/pronouns/{object,placement,possessives,possessive-vs-article}
/practice/verbs                                  Verb index (4 phases)
/practice/verbs/present/{vocabulary,conjugations,irregular,eimai,full}
/practice/verbs/past/{aorist-vocabulary,aorist-stems,aorist-formation,imperfect-stative,aorist-conjugation}
/practice/verbs/future/{vocabulary,formation,conjugation}
/practice/verbs/{modal-constructions,imperatives,ladder,tense-recognition}
/practice/blocks                                 Building-blocks index (flat list)
/practice/blocks/{chunks,numbers,days-of-week,opposites}
/practice/blocks/question-words                  Question-words index (4 phases)
/practice/blocks/question-words/{basics,which-forms,which-phrase,how-many-forms,how-many-phrase,review}
```

Route segments use grammatical terms (`nominative`); drill titles and phase labels use the learner handles (Doer / Target / Owner).

## Landing Page

<route path="/practice">
<purpose>Hub: one link per drill group; no drills are listed here</purpose>
<file>src/routes/practice/index.tsx</file>
<displays>
- A ruled list built from `SECTIONS`, each row a serif label plus a one-line thesis:
  - The case system → /practice/cases
  - Pronouns → /practice/pronouns
  - Verbs → /practice/verbs
  - Building blocks → /practice/blocks
</displays>
</route>

<route path="/practice/review">
<purpose>Drills whose rust score says they need attention</purpose>
<file>src/routes/practice/review.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Loader `getReviewDrillsFn` calls `getSchemaRust(userId)` (`src/server/db/queries/analytics/drill-stats.ts`) and keeps drills found in `DRILL_REGISTRY`.
- Rows grouped under `DRILL_CATEGORY_LABELS` (`src/constants/drills.ts`): title, rust bar, days since and accuracy. "All caught up" state when empty.
</displays>
</route>

## Drill catalogue

<source-of-truth>
Each group owns its entries in `practice/<group>/drills.data.ts`: `cases` → `CASE_PHASES`, `verbs` → `VERB_PHASES`, `pronouns` → `PRONOUN_DRILLS`, `blocks` → `BLOCK_DRILLS` (plus `QUESTION_WORDS_LINK`, a link row that records nothing), `blocks/question-words` → `QUESTION_WORD_PHASES`.
`drill-catalogue.data.ts` derives `DRILL_REGISTRY` (keyed by drill id) and `drillTitle(drillId)` from those lists; never author entries there. A `DrillEntry` (`src/constants/drills.ts`) has `id` (the `drillId` attempts are recorded under), `to`, `title`, `greek` sample, `minutes`, `category`, `caseRole`.
</source-of-truth>

Group indexes render `DrillIndex` (`components/drill-index.tsx`) with `phases` or a flat `drills` list. Phase headers take `PHASE_TINT`: Doer / Target / Owner use the reserved case tokens via `SCHEME["case-nominative" | "case-accusative" | "case-genitive"]`; Review and every other phase (verb tenses, question-word phases) are muted neutral.

## Section: The case system

`CASE_PHASES`, rendered by `cases/index.tsx`. Each role phase has the same four drills, Article → Noun → Adjective → Phrase, then a Review phase mixes cases.

```
DOER     Article (Doer)      ο · η · το · οι · τα                 generated from getArticle
         Noun (Doer)         ο φίλος · η θάλασσα · το σπίτι       DB, SRS pool
         Adjective (Doer)    καλός · καλή · καλό                  hand-curated, 60 forms
         Phrase (Doer)       ο καλός φίλος                        hand-curated, 30 phrases
TARGET   Article / Noun / Adjective (60) / Phrase (30)            τον · τη · το · τους · τις · τα
OWNER    Article / Noun / Adjective (40) / Phrase (30)            του · της · του · των
REVIEW   All articles        18 forms, multi-select reverse (gender, number, case)
         All nouns           DB, every nominal_forms cell, VocabDrillPage
         All adjectives      DB, every nominal_forms cell, VocabDrillPage
         All phrases         the three phrase lists combined, reverse = pick the case
```

<engine-notes>
- Articles: `cases/components/article-drill.tsx` (`CaseArticleDrill`) builds the six cells from `getArticle` (`src/lib/greek-grammar.ts`), with per-cell `overrides` (Target f-sg drills τη and accepts την via `acceptAlso`) and a `Paradigm` table as `configExtras`.
- Nouns: loader calls `getNounDrillItemsFn` (`src/server/fns/noun.ts`): pool from `getDrillVocabPool` (`src/server/db/queries/drill-pool.ts`, CEFR band via `adjacentCefrPool`, limit 50), singular form of the case from `getVocabularyWithNominalForms`. Reverse is single-select on gender; only Doer strips the article for reverse.
- Adjectives: Owner has 40 forms because plural -ων is one item for all genders (reverse option "Plural · any gender", `NEUTRAL`).
- Review nouns / adjectives: loader calls `getNominalReviewQuestionsFn` (`src/server/fns/cases.ts`, limit 45), one question per `nominal_forms` cell with a "(Doer, sg, m)" style hint.
- Review phrases imports `PHRASES` from the three phrase routes and re-tags each item by case.
- `themeFor` in `engines/drill.tsx`: a drill whose `caseRole` is doer / target / owner takes the reserved case tokens for its bar and selectors; `mixed` and `null` use the `colorTheme` prop (base palette, default terracotta).
</engine-notes>

## Section: Pronouns

`PRONOUN_DRILLS`, a flat list on `pronouns/index.tsx`:

- Object pronouns (`object.tsx`) and Possessive pronouns (`possessives.tsx`): hand-curated paradigms, `ForwardPromptCard` prompts, multi-select reverse, `Paradigm` table before the session, `sessionSize={10}`.
- Pronoun placement (`placement.tsx`): forward-only word ordering; items and categories in `placement.data.ts`; `sessionSize={20}`.
- Whose, or of the? (`possessive-vs-article.tsx`): ο πατέρας του against ο πατέρας του παιδιού; items in `possessive-vs-article.data.ts`; opens in reverse, single-select on the word's role.

## Section: Verbs

`VERB_PHASES`, four phases on `verbs/index.tsx` (route segments shown):

```
PRESENT          present/vocabulary* · present/conjugations · present/irregular · present/eimai · present/full*
PAST             past/aorist-vocabulary* · past/aorist-stems · past/aorist-formation · present/conjugations · past/imperfect-stative · past/aorist-conjugation*
FUTURE & MODAL   future/vocabulary* · future/formation · future/conjugation* · modal-constructions · imperatives
MIXED TENSES     ladder* · tense-recognition*
```

`*` = DB-driven: loader calls `getVerbDrillQuestionsFn` (`src/server/fns/verbs.ts`, queries in `verbs.server.ts`) and renders `VocabDrillPage`. The vocabulary drills ask sg1 only; Which tense? reverses to a single-select on `TENSE_DIMENSION_OPTIONS`. Conjugation endings is one `DrillEntry` (`CONJUGATION_ENDINGS`) listed under both Present and Past. The rest are hand-curated item lists inside each route file.

## Section: Building blocks

`BLOCK_DRILLS` plus `QUESTION_WORDS_LINK`, a flat list on `blocks/index.tsx`: Survival phrases (`chunks`), Numbers, Days & time, Opposites, Question words. Opposites is DB-driven (`getOppositePairsFn`); the rest are hand-curated. Question words is a sub-group with its own index and six drills. Each has a `*.content.llm` beside its route.

## Drill engine

<engine-notes>
Files in `components/engines/`:
- `drill.tsx`: `<Drill>`, the engine every drill uses. Props include `drillId`, `items`, `title` (omit it; the catalogue title is used), `colorTheme`, `defaultMode`, `reverse` (`self-assess` by default, `single-select`, `multi-select`), `forwardPrompt`, `configExtras`, `autoStart`, `sessionSize` (10 / 20 / 30, or an exact count such as /try's), `speed` (preselects a speed; the only way to set one when `autoStart` skips the config screen), `onComplete`, `summaryFooter`, plus `ConfigShell` copy props (`subtitle`, `forwardDesc`, `reverseDesc`, `categories`, `forwardOnly`, `referenceHref`, `backTo`).
- `vocab-drill.tsx`: `VocabDrillPage` maps server `DrillQuestion[]` to forms and renders `<Drill>` with `sessionSize={20}`.
- `shells.tsx`: `ConfigShell` (filter, mode, card count, speed, Begin), `DrillShell` (top bar), `ForwardInput`, `FeedbackDisplay` and `ReverseFeedback` (both inside `FeedbackFrame`), `SummaryScreen`.
- `drill-hooks.ts`: `useCountdown`, `useForwardKeyboard`, `useContinueKeyboard`, `useCardState`. `drill-store.ts`: zustand `useDrillStore` and `drillActions`.
- `deck.ts`: `DrillForm`, `SimpleListItem`, `SESSION_SIZES`, `buildWeightedDeck` (interleaves SRS buckets; a new word reappears about five cards later).
- `reverse/`: `SelfAssessReverse`, `SingleSelectReverse`, `MultiSelectReverse`. `drill-constants.ts` and `chip-specs.ts`: shared selector options (gender ones take the reserved gender tokens; person and tense ones are `NEUTRAL`) and prompt chips.

Behaviour:
- Top bar (`DrillShell`): Exit link, the drill title as the page `h1`, "N of M". Bucket and "remediation ×N" chips show only for a logged-in user (`userId > 0`), so never on /try.
- Timing: the learner's Fast 4 s / Medium 6 s (default) / Relaxed 8 s choice (`drill-speeds.ts`). In forward mode each extra word in the answer adds 35% (`scaleTimeLimitForPhrase`). A timeout records a miss.
- Grading: `matchPhonetic` (`src/lib/greek-transliteration.ts`) against `greek`, then `acceptAlso`. It accepts the answer with or without a leading article and strips terminal `;` `?` `!` `.` on both sides.
- Keys: a blank Enter is ignored and records nothing. Enter or Space continues after any feedback; a correct answer also advances by itself after 1200 ms, a wrong one waits (or tap the feedback block). Keys pressed in another control (header search, a focused button or link) are left to that control; the answer input submits through its own form and still continues on Enter or Space.
- Remediation: a missed card is re-inserted about five cards later, at most three times per word.
- `SummaryScreen`: "N of M correct" as the `h1`, with accuracy and average time; "Missed this round" lists each missed word and what was typed; "Drill the N you missed" (a re-drill that records no attempts) then "Practice again". Focus moves to the first action button. `summaryFooter` renders below the actions. With `autoStart`, "Practice again" restarts at once instead of returning to config.
- Attempts are recorded through `src/server/fns/srs.ts` (`startSessionFn`, `recordAttemptFn`, `completeSessionFn`) only for a logged-in user.
</engine-notes>

## Educational principle

Each case phase mirrors the production-skill operation a learner performs at speed:
- Bare form (Article): function-word retrieval
- Single-class application (Noun, Adjective): morphology
- Phrase integration (Phrase): full noun-phrase production

Asymmetric content reflects honest priority. Don't symmetrise where frequency disagrees: `how-many-phrase` leaves out genitive πόσου/πόσης because it is rare in modern speech.

## Data sources

- **Hand-curated drill content**: inside each route file (e.g. `cases/nominative/adjective.tsx`) or a sibling `*.data.ts` (`pronouns/placement.data.ts`, `pronouns/possessive-vs-article.data.ts`).
- **Vocabulary + cases**: seeded into `vocabulary` + `nominal_forms` via `src/scripts/seed.ts`. `src/scripts/seed-data/vocabulary/noun-seed-enrichment.ts` calls `declineNoun` for every (case × number) cell; `adjective-seed-enrichment.ts` calls `declineAdjective` for (case × number × gender).
- **Verb conjugations and opposites**: the same `seed.ts` calls `seedVerbConjugations()` and `seedOpposites()`.

See `src/server/db/CLAUDE.md` for query patterns.
